# :normal and :{range}normal (various.txt), with macros.

=== :normal runs Normal mode commands
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  Execute Normal mode commands {commands}.
given:  |abcdef
keys:   :normal 2x<CR>
expect: |cdef
mode:   normal

=== :norm runs keys like they are typed
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  {commands} are executed like they are typed.
given:  |one two three
keys:   :norm wdw<CR>
expect: one |three
mode:   normal

=== :normal finishes an unfinished insert as if <Esc> was typed
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  If {commands} does not finish a command, the last one will be aborted as if <Esc> or <C-C> was typed.
given:  |x
keys:   :normal Afoo<CR>
expect: xfo|o
mode:   normal

=== :normal drops an unfinished operator
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  If {commands} does not finish a command, the last one will be aborted as if <Esc> or <C-C> was typed.
given:  |one two
keys:   :normal d<CR>
expect: |one two
mode:   normal

=== :normal stops at the first error
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  Execution stops when an error is encountered.
given:  |abcd
keys:   :normal fzx<CR>
expect: |abcd
mode:   normal

=== u undoes all of :normal at once
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  For undo all commands are undone together.
given:  |abcdef
keys:   :normal xxx<CR>
expect: |def
undo:   |abcdef
mode:   normal

=== :normal uses mappings
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  If the [!] is given, mappings will not be used.
given:
  |abc
  two
keys:   :nmap x dd<CR>:normal x<CR>
expect: |two
mode:   normal

=== :normal! ignores mappings
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  If the [!] is given, mappings will not be used.
given:
  |abc
  two
keys:   :nmap x dd<CR>:normal! x<CR>
expect:
  |bc
  two
mode:   normal

=== :normal 1 x starts with a space through a count
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  {commands} cannot start with a space.  Put a count of 1 (one) before it, "1 " is one space.
given:  |abc
keys:   :normal 1 x<CR>
expect: a|c
mode:   normal

=== :normal runs a macro
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  Execute Normal mode commands {commands}.
given:  |abcdef
keys:   qaxq:normal 2@a<CR>
expect: |def
mode:   normal

=== :normal runs an Ex command finished with <CR>
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  A ":" command must be completed as well.
given:
  |a1
  a2
keys:   :exe "normal :s/a/b/\<lt>CR>j"<CR>
expect:
  b1
  |a2
mode:   normal

=== :normal drops an unfinished : command
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  A ":" command must be completed as well.
given:  |a1
keys:   :normal :s/a/b/<CR>
expect: |a1
mode:   normal

=== :%normal runs the keys on every line
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal-range*
quote:  Execute Normal mode commands {commands} for each line in the {range}.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :%normal A;<CR>
expect:
  one;
  two;
  three|;
mode:   normal

=== :{range}normal starts each line at the first column
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal-range*
quote:  Before executing the {commands}, the cursor is positioned in the first column of the range, for each line.
given:
  abc
  a|bc
  abc
  abc
keys:   :2,3normal x<CR>
expect:
  abc
  bc
  |bc
  abc
mode:   normal

=== :{range}normal with a count
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal-range*
quote:  Otherwise it's the same as the ":normal" command without a range.
given:
  |abcd
  abcd
keys:   :%normal 2x<CR>
expect:
  cd
  |cd
mode:   normal

=== :{range}normal! ignores mappings on every line
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal-range*
quote:  Execute Normal mode commands {commands} for each line in the {range}.
given:
  |abc
  abc
keys:   :nmap x dd<CR>:%normal! x<CR>
expect:
  bc
  |bc
mode:   normal

=== :{range}normal runs a macro on every line
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal-range*
quote:  Execute Normal mode commands {commands} for each line in the {range}.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   qaI- <Esc>q:2,$normal @a<CR>
expect:
  - one
  - two
  -| three
mode:   normal

=== an error on one line of :{range}normal doesn't stop the others
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal-range*
quote:  Otherwise it's the same as the ":normal" command without a range.
given:
  |a.b
  ab
  a.b
keys:   :%normal f.x<CR>
expect:
  ab
  ab
  a|b
mode:   normal

=== :'<,'>normal runs on the lines of the Visual area
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal-range*
quote:  Execute Normal mode commands {commands} for each line in the {range}.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   Vj:normal I#<CR>
expect:
  #one
  |#two
  three
mode:   normal

=== u undoes all lines of :{range}normal at once
ref:    nvim/various.txt *:normal*
quote:  For undo all commands are undone together.
given:
  |abc
  abc
keys:   :%normal x<CR>
expect:
  bc
  |bc
undo:
  |abc
  abc
mode:   normal
